      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `URLCodec_ESTest_test01.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-codec/auto/testcases/URLCodec_ESTest/URLCodec_ESTest_test01.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `URLCodec.decodeUrl()` throws a `DecoderException` when the input byte array ends with a bare `%` (ASCII 37) escape character with no following hex digits. I'll improve clarity by renaming the variable, using a character literal instead of a raw magic number, removing the unused `BitSet` import, and adding a meaningful comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: renamed `byteArray0` to `bytesEndingWithPercentSign` for clarity, replaced the magic number `(byte) 37` with `(byte) '%'` to make the intent obvious, removed the unused `BitSet` import, and added a Javadoc comment and inline comments explaining why the exception is expected."
    }
